      "text": "To find the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285, we need to find the greatest common divisor (GCD) of 342 and 285. Let's follow these steps:\n\n1. **Prime Factorization**:\n   - Start with the prime factorization of 342:\n     \\[\n     342 \\div 2 = 171 \\quad \\text{(342 is even, so it is divisible by 2)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     171 \\div 3 = 57 \\quad \\text{(sum of digits of 171 is 9, which is divisible by 3)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     57 \\div 3 = 19 \\quad \\text{(sum of digits of 57 is 12, which is divisible by 3)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     19 \\div 19 = 1 \\quad \\text{(19 is a prime number)}\n     \\]\n     So, the prime factorization of 342 is:\n     \\[\n     342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19\n     \\]\n\n   - Now, let's factorize 285:\n     \\[\n     285 \\div 3 = 95 \\quad \\text{(sum of digits of 285 is 15, which is divisible by 3)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     95 \\div 5 = 19 \\quad \\text{(95 ends in 5, so it is divisible by 5)}\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     19 \\div 19 = 1 \\quad \\text{(19 is a prime number)}\n     \\]\n     So, the prime factorization of 285 is:\n     \\[\n     285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19\n     \\]\n\n2. **Common Divisors**:\n   - Identify the common prime factors of 342 and 285:\n     \\[\n     342 = 2 \\times 3^2 \\times 19\n     \\]\n     \\[\n     285 = 3 \\times 5 \\times 19\n     \\]\n   - The common prime factors are 3 and 19. The lowest powers of these common prime factors are:\n     \\[\n     3^1 \\quad \\text{and} \\quad 19^1\n     \\]\n   - Therefore, the greatest common divisor (GCD) is:\n     \\[\n     \\text{GCD} = 3^1 \\times 19^1 = 3 \\times 19 = 57\n     \\]\n\nThus, the largest divisor of 342 that is also a factor of 285 is \\(\\boxed{57}\\).",
